  "about": "Counts per official rulebook: entries in the book, entries DAS · Core covers with a dedicated entry (`core`), entries das-rulepack covers (`rulepack`). Counts only: no names of entries, no text.",
  "method": "Static comparison by name. Each entry of a book's catalogue (spells, feats, optional features, items, class and subclass features, monsters) is counted once, under the book the catalogue files it in; its name, turned into a dnd5e-style identifier, is looked up among the identifiers of DAS · Core, then among those of das-rulepack (an entry found in both is counted under `core`). A dedicated entry is not proof that the rule works, and no entry does not mean it does not: much is resolved from the item's own data.",
